#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld
msgid "# **Logical Equivalences**\n"
"Let §0 and §1 be propositions (§2). We say that §3 is **logically equivalent** to §4 to mean that §5, in other words, §6 is true whenever §7 is true, moreover, §8 is false whenever §9 is false. To put it succinctly, the truth tables for §10 and §11 are identical. Here are a few well-known logical equivalences that we can check via truth-tables:\n"
"* **Conditional Law:** §12\n"
"* **Commutative Law:** §13 and §14\n"
"* **Associative Law:** §15 and §16\n"
"* **DeMorgan's Law:** §17 and §18.\n"
"\n"
"The purpose of this world is to practice writing proofs of logical equivalences *using* known logical equivalences (like those above and others we'll learn about). Let's get started!"
msgstr ""

