#. §4: ```
#. mem_inter_iff
#.   {u : Type*}
#.   (x : u)
#.   (a b : Set u) :
#.     x ∈ a ∩ b ↔ x ∈ a ∧ x ∈ b
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.set_docs
#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.set_docs
msgid "This helps to define the §0 set connective. Specifically,\n"
"§1\n"
"So §2 says specifically that §3. Here's how it looks in Lean:\n"
"§4"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.ArgWorld_eg.L02_arg
msgid "### **Level 2**\n"
"This argument is sometimes called the law of **Conditional Proof**. It might help to apply a"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∧`
#. §1: $$ (P ∧ Q) ∧ R ↔ P ∧ (Q ∧ R) $$
#. §2: `And_assoc`
#. §3: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|ccc||cc|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & R & (P ∧ Q) ∧ R & P ∧ (Q ∧ R) \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T & T & T \\
#.   T & T & F & F & F \\
#.   T & F & T & F & F \\
#.   T & F & F & F & F \\
#.   F & T & T & F & F \\
#.   F & T & F & F & F \\
#.   F & F & T & F & F \\
#.   F & F & F & F & F \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
msgid "This is the **Associative Law** for §0. It says that\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"The proof of §2 is given in the truth-table below:\n"
"§3"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.ArgWorld_eg.L02_arg
msgid "Conditional Proof"
